    "expect_exit": 0,
    "expect_stdout": "",
    "parity": false,
    "parity_exception": "PE-20",
    "_note": "PE-20 (owner-directed, live-harness-forced removal): the Claude Code hooks docs state PostCompact stdout is never shown to the model (injected only for UserPromptSubmit/UserPromptExpansion/SessionStart/PostModelSwitch) and PostCompact carries no output channel of any shape -- there was never anything the JSON envelope this fixture used to pin could have delivered. The anchor is already redelivered after compaction via SessionStart(source=compact), which fires with real stdout injection, so dispatch.events.PostCompact was redundant and is now DELETED from config.json (not repaired). This fixture exercises dispatch() itself (not skill_anchor.run() directly, via \"via\": \"dispatch_route\") to prove PostCompact resolves to zero rules and produces no output -- a re-added registration would fail this case. The retired .ps1 master had this same dead registration (it fired stdout no harness ever surfaced); this is a deliberate divergence away from that, not a port error."
  },
